ry observations must be judged against a fixed acceptance contract)\nLoaded: presume (when: \"make a call and move on\" — not: \"guess and adjust\" — because: reversible interpretation choices should not interrupt the requested independent review)\nLoaded: atomic (when: \"one thing per step\" — not: \"don't bundle changes\" — because: each inspection or verification action must yield one independently attributable observation)\nLoads verified: witness, full, ground, presume, atomic (5 of 5)\nToken loads complete.\n\nToken derivations:\n[witness]: \"architecture review\" → \"The response names each assumption and its epistemic basis in the same paragraph or numbered step before stating any conclusion that depends on it\" as applied here: each verdict will cite the contract or independently regenerated observation on which it rests.\n[full]: \"cover everything important\" → \"The response addresses every named element of the subject at one level of depth\" as applied here: the review matrix will cover every criterion in the request exactly once.\n[ground]: \"derive what correctness means before acting\" → \"The response must produce a 'Ground properties:' block before any test, implementation step, tool call, or task reasoning begins\" as applied here: formal acceptance properties are fixed below before repository inspection.\nWhat it requires here: derive a complete, non-overlapping acceptance predicate from the user’s explicit package, custody, interface, wiring, stage, scope, and reproducibility requirements.\n[presume]: \"make a call and move on\" → \"The response selects the most plausible option wherever the subject leaves a choice open and proceeds on it instead of stopping to request approval or clarification\" as applied here: ambiguous document labels will be resolved by exact package-local references and revised if repository evidence contradicts that reading.\nWhat it requires here: state each reversible interpretive choice and its contradiction trigger.\n[atomic]: \"one thing per step\" → \"The response makes one observable change per step, where a step is a single unit of change\" as applied here: each read-only command will have a single evidentiary purpose and no command will mutate the target.\nWhat it requires here: separate provenance, document, dependency, checksum, compile, vet, call-site, and visibility observations.\nCombined stance: without witness, the final token would not be reconstructible from cited observations; without full, named criteria could disappear into a summary; without ground, observations could silently redefine acceptance; without presume, harmless label ambiguity could stall the review; without atomic, failures could not be attributed to one verification boundary.\nDerived stance complete.\n\nGround properties:\nInterpretation: acceptance means the exact committed package at `acf563e7` satisfies every expressly named contract and scope constraint, and fresh disposable verification independently reproduces its claimed mechanical status; the accessible-observation boundary is the committed source/docs plus outputs generated by read-only checks in a disposable location.\nproperty [1]: ∀p, Accept(p) ⇒ ExactRevision(p, acf563e7) ∧ SourcesMatch(p,{lease-source-V2,C15-two-stage,generic-amendment,blocked-v1,blocked-v2,source/write-set}) ∧ RecomputedDepsChecksumsStatus(p)\n§ formality check: property [1]: \"∀p, Accept(p) ⇒ ExactRevision(p, acf563e7) ∧ SourcesMatch(p,{lease-source-V2,C15-two-stage,generic-amendment,blocked-v1,blocked-v2,source/write-set}) ∧ RecomputedDepsChecksumsStatus(p)\" — formal\n§ minimality: property [1]: minimal — most specific sub-term: \"acf563e7\"; candidate relaxation: replace \"acf563e7\" with any revision; rejected: the requester fixed that exact HEAD.\nproperty [1a]: ∀p, Accept(p) ⇒ ExactRevision(p,acf563e7)\nproperty [1b]: ∀p, Accept(p) ⇒ SourcesMatch(p,S) ∧ RecomputedDepsChecksumsStatus(p)\n§ formality check: property [1a]: \"∀p, Accept(p) ⇒ ExactRevision(p,acf563e7)\" — formal\n§ formality check: property [1b]: \"∀p, Accept(p) ⇒ SourcesMatch(p,S) ∧ RecomputedDepsChecksumsStatus(p)\" — formal\n§ split test: property [1]: \"∀p, Accept(p) ⇒ ExactRevision(p, acf563e7) ∧ SourcesMatch(p,{lease-source-V2,C15-two-stage,generic-amendment,blocked-v1,blocked-v2,source/write-set}) ∧ RecomputedDepsChecksumsStatus(p)\" ⇔ (property [1a]: \"∀p, Accept(p) ⇒ ExactRevision(p,acf563e7)\" ∧ property [1b]: \"∀p, Accept(p) ⇒ SourcesMatch(p,S) ∧ RecomputedDepsChecksumsStatus(p)\"); property [1a] — falsified by the same package at another revision; property [1b] — falsified by the exact revision with a source mismatch; these falsifiers are independent.\n§ constraint coverage: property [1]: covers {exact worktree HEAD, accepted source set, recomputed dependency/checksum/status evidence}\n§ atomic: property [1]: \"∀p, Accept(p) ⇒ ExactRevision(p, acf563e7) ∧ SourcesMatch(p,{lease-source-V2,C15-two-stage,generic-amendment,blocked-v1,blocked-v2,source/write-set}) ∧ RecomputedDepsChecksumsStatus(p)\" — candidate split rejected: these are one package-identity/provenance constraint at the request’s acceptance granularity.\n\nproperty [2]: ∀r∈RawBuffers, OneManagerSubledger(r) ∧ ReserveBeforeCopy(r) ∧ NoLeaseEscape(r) ∧ AtomicSingleOwnerTransfer(r) ∧ TerminalConvergenceRelease(r) ∧ LockOrder(r)=L₁≺L₂≺L₃ ∧ ¬LockInversion(r)\n§ formality check: property [2]: \"∀r∈RawBuffers, OneManagerSubledger(r) ∧ ReserveBeforeCopy(r) ∧ NoLeaseEscape(r) ∧ AtomicSingleOwnerTransfer(r) ∧ TerminalConvergenceRelease(r) ∧ LockOrder(r)=L₁≺L₂≺L₃ ∧ ¬LockInversion(r)\" — formal\n§ minimality: property [2]: minimal — most specific sub-term: \"L₁≺L₂≺L₃\"; candidate relaxation: replace \"L₁≺L₂≺L₃\" with an arbitrary order; rejected: the requester requires the full three-lock order and no inversion.\nproperty [2a]: ∀r, OneManagerSubledger(r) ∧ ReserveBeforeCopy(r) ∧ NoLeaseEscape(r)\nproperty [2b]: ∀r, AtomicSingleOwnerTransfer(r) ∧ TerminalConvergenceRelease(r) ∧ LockOrder(r)=L₁≺L₂≺L₃ ∧ ¬LockInversion(r)\n§ formality check: property [2a]: \"∀r, OneManagerSubledger(r) ∧ ReserveBeforeCopy(r) ∧ NoLeaseEscape(r)\" — formal\n§ formality check: property [2b]: \"∀r, AtomicSingleOwnerTransfer(r) ∧ TerminalConvergenceRelease(r) ∧ LockOrder(r)=L₁≺L₂≺L₃ ∧ ¬LockInversion(r)\" — formal\n§ split test: property [2]: \"∀r∈RawBuffers, OneManagerSubledger(r) ∧ ReserveBeforeCopy(r) ∧ NoLeaseEscape(r) ∧ AtomicSingleOwnerTransfer(r) ∧ TerminalConvergenceRelease(r) ∧ LockOrder(r)=L₁≺L₂≺L₃ ∧ ¬LockInversion(r)\" ⇔ (property [2a]: \"∀r, OneManagerSubledger(r) ∧ ReserveBeforeCopy(r) ∧ NoLeaseEscape(r)\" ∧ property [2b]: \"∀r, AtomicSingleOwnerTransfer(r) ∧ TerminalConvergenceRelease(r) ∧ LockOrder(r)=L₁≺L₂≺L₃ ∧ ¬LockInversion(r)\"); property [2a] — falsified by duplicate accounting with correct transfer/locks; property [2b] — falsified by lock inversion with correct accounting; these falsifiers are independent.\n§ constraint coverage: property [2]: covers {single Manager subledger/account source, reservation before every copy including exact and +1, no lease-bearing escape, atomic one-owner transfer, terminal convergence/release, complete three-lock order, no inversion}\n§ atomic: property [2]: \"∀r∈RawBuffers, OneManagerSubledger(r) ∧ ReserveBeforeCopy(r) ∧ NoLeaseEscape(r) ∧ AtomicSingleOwnerTransfer(r) ∧ TerminalConvergenceRelease(r) ∧ LockOrder(r)=L₁≺L₂≺L₃ ∧ ¬LockInversion(r)\" — candidate split rejected: the request identifies these collectively as one custody invariant.\n\nproperty [3]: Components(p)=SixNamedComponents ∧ |Components(p)|=6 ∧ AliasCount(p)=0\n§ formality check: property [3]: \"Components(p)=SixNamedComponents ∧ |Components(p)|=6 ∧ AliasCount(p)=0\" — formal\n§ minimality: property [3]: minimal — most specific sub-term: \"6\"; candidate relaxation: replace \"6\" with another cardinality; rejected: the requester explicitly requires all six and zero aliases.\nproperty [3a]: Components(p)=SixNamedComponents ∧ |Components(p)|=6\nproperty [3b]: AliasCount(p)=0\n§ formality check: property [3a]: \"Components(p)=SixNamedComponents ∧ |Components(p)|=6\" — formal\n§ formality check: property [3b]: \"AliasCount(p)=0\" — formal\n§ split test: property [3]: \"Components(p)=SixNamedComponents ∧ |Components(p)|=6 ∧ AliasCount(p)=0\" ⇔ (property [3a]: \"Components(p)=SixNamedComponents ∧ |Components(p)|=6\" ∧ property [3b]: \"AliasCount(p)=0\"); property [3a] — falsified by five components and no aliases; property [3b] — falsified by six components plus one alias; these falsifiers are independent.\n§ constraint coverage: property [3]: covers {all six components, zero aliases}\n§ atomic: property [3]: \"Components(p)=SixNamedComponents ∧ |Components(p)|=6 ∧ AliasCount(p)=0\" — candidate split rejected: cardinality and alias absence jointly define the requested exact component set.\n\nproperty [4]: ∀q∈Profiles, Independent(q) ∧ TargetComplete(q) ∧ Fields(q)=ExactFields ∧ Signatures(q)=ExactSignatures ∧ NilErrorRefusal(q)=ExactContract\n§ formality check: property [4]: \"∀q∈Profiles, Independent(q) ∧ TargetComplete(q) ∧ Fields(q)=ExactFields ∧ Signatures(q)=ExactSignatures ∧ NilErrorRefusal(q)=ExactContract\" — formal\n§ minimality: property [4]: minimal — most specific sub-term: \"ExactSignatures\"; candidate relaxation: replace \"ExactSignatures\" with signature compatibility; rejected: exact signatures are expressly required.\nproperty [4a]: ∀q, Independent(q) ∧ TargetComplete(q)\nproperty [4b]: ∀q, Fields(q)=ExactFields ∧ Signatures(q)=ExactSignatures ∧ NilErrorRefusal(q)=ExactContract\n§ formality check: property [4a]: \"∀q, Independent(q) ∧ TargetComplete(q)\" — formal\n§ formality check: property [4b]: \"∀q, Fields(q)=ExactFields ∧ Signatures(q)=ExactSignatures ∧ NilErrorRefusal(q)=ExactContract\" — formal\n§ split test: property [4]: \"∀q∈Profiles, Independent(q) ∧ TargetComplete(q) ∧ Fields(q)=ExactFields ∧ Signatures(q)=ExactSignatures ∧ NilErrorRefusal(q)=ExactContract\" ⇔ (property [4a]: \"∀q, Independent(q) ∧ TargetComplete(q)\" ∧ property [4b]: \"∀q, Fields(q)=ExactFields ∧ Signatures(q)=ExactSignatures ∧ NilErrorRefusal(q)=ExactContract\"); property [4a] — falsified by a target-incomplete profile with exact API; property [4b] — falsified by a complete profile with a wrong signature; these falsifiers are independent.\n§ constraint coverage: property [4]: covers {generic independent profiles, target completeness, exact fields, exact signatures, nil/error/refusal behavior}\n§ atomic: property [4]: \"∀q∈Profiles, Independent(q) ∧ TargetComplete(q) ∧ Fields(q)=ExactFields ∧ Signatures(q)=ExactSignatures ∧ NilErrorRefusal(q)=ExactContract\" — candidate split rejected: these jointly define the generic private-interface contract.\n\nproperty [5]: WiredIDs(p)=PlannedIDs₂₀ ∧ Stage(p)=B_Postimplementation ∧ Scope(p)=SixPlusFour ∧ ¬Drift(p,{Expansion,gopls,Public,D-R,CALLS_ONLY})\n§ formality check: property [5]: \"WiredIDs(p)=PlannedIDs₂₀ ∧ Stage(p)=B_Postimplementation ∧ Scope(p)=SixPlusFour ∧ ¬Drift(p,{Expansion,gopls,Public,D-R,CALLS_ONLY})\" — formal\n§ minimality: property [5]: minimal — most specific sub-term: \"PlannedIDs₂₀\"; candidate relaxation: replace \"PlannedIDs₂₀\" with a subset; rejected: all 20 planned IDs are expressly required.\nproperty [5a]: WiredIDs(p)=PlannedIDs₂₀ ∧ Stage(p)=B_Postimplementation\nproperty [5b]: Scope(p)=SixPlusFour ∧ ¬Drift(p,{Expansion,gopls,Public,D-R,CALLS_ONLY})\n§ formality check: property [5a]: \"WiredIDs(p)=PlannedIDs₂₀ ∧ Stage(p)=B_Postimplementation\" — formal\n§ formality check: property [5b]: \"Scope(p)=SixPlusFour ∧ ¬Drift(p,{Expansion,gopls,Public,D-R,CALLS_ONLY})\" — formal\n§ split test: property [5]: \"WiredIDs(p)=PlannedIDs₂₀ ∧ Stage(p)=B_Postimplementation ∧ Scope(p)=SixPlusFour ∧ ¬Drift(p,{Expansion,gopls,Public,D-R,CALLS_ONLY})\" ⇔ (property [5a]: \"WiredIDs(p)=PlannedIDs₂₀ ∧ Stage(p)=B_Postimplementation\" ∧ property [5b]: \"Scope(p)=SixPlusFour ∧ ¬Drift(p,{Expansion,gopls,Public,D-R,CALLS_ONLY})\"); property [5a] — falsified by one unwired ID with correct scope; property [5b] — falsified by public/gopls expansion with all IDs wired; these falsifiers are independent.\n§ constraint coverage: property [5]: covers {20 planned IDs wired, Stage B postimplementation, exact six-plus-four scope, no expansion, no gopls, no public surface, no D-R drift, no CALLS_ONLY drift}\n§ atomic: property [5]: \"WiredIDs(p)=PlannedIDs₂₀ ∧ Stage(p)=B_Postimplementation ∧ Scope(p)=SixPlusFour ∧ ¬Drift(p,{Expansion,gopls,Public,D-R,CALLS_ONLY})\" — candidate split rejected: these jointly define the requested closed implementation scope.\n\nproperty [6]: ∃h, Disposable(h) ∧ Fresh(h) ∧ CompileOK(h) ∧ VetOK(h) ∧ AllCallSitesOK(h) ∧ PrivateVisibilityOK(h)\n§ formality check: property [6]: \"∃h, Disposable(h) ∧ Fresh(h) ∧ CompileOK(h) ∧ VetOK(h) ∧ AllCallSitesOK(h) ∧ PrivateVisibilityOK(h)\" — formal\n§ minimality: property [6]: minimal — most specific sub-term: \"PrivateVisibilityOK\"; candidate relaxation: omit \"PrivateVisibilityOK\"; rejected: the requester explicitly requires private-visibility verification.\nproperty [6a]: ∃h, Disposable(h) ∧ Fresh(h) ∧ CompileOK(h) ∧ VetOK(h)\nproperty [6b]: ∃h, AllCallSitesOK(h) ∧ PrivateVisibilityOK(h)\n§ formality check: property [6a]: \"∃h, Disposable(h) ∧ Fresh(h) ∧ CompileOK(h) ∧ VetOK(h)\" — formal\n§ formality check: property [6b]: \"∃h, AllCallSitesOK(h) ∧ PrivateVisibilityOK(h)\" — formal\n§ split test: property [6]: \"∃h, Disposable(h) ∧ Fresh(h) ∧ CompileOK(h) ∧ VetOK(h) ∧ AllCallSitesOK(h) ∧ PrivateVisibilityOK(h)\" ⇔ (property [6a]: \"∃h, Disposable(h) ∧ Fresh(h) ∧ CompileOK(h) ∧ VetOK(h)\" ∧ property [6b]: \"∃h, AllCallSitesOK(h) ∧ PrivateVisibilityOK(h)\"); property [6a] — falsified by compile failure despite call-site/visibility success; property [6b] — falsified by a public leak despite compile/vet success; these falsifiers are independent.\n§ constraint coverage: property [6]: covers {fresh disposable harness, compile, vet, all call sites, private visibility}\n§ atomic: property [6]: \"∃h, Disposable(h) ∧ Fresh(h) ∧ CompileOK(h) ∧ VetOK(h) ∧ AllCallSitesOK(h) ∧ PrivateVisibilityOK(h)\" — candidate split rejected: these collectively define the expressly requested independent rebuild outcome.\n\n§ completeness check: \"Review package ... against accepted lease-source V2 and two-stage C15 contract, generic amendment, blocked v1/v2, source/write-set. Recompute deps/checksums/status and independently rebuild fresh disposable harness/compile/vet/all call sites/private visibility. Verify exact Manager subledger/account source/no second owner; all six components+zero aliases; reservation before every copy/exact/+1; lease-bearing no escape; atomic transfer one owner; terminal convergence/release; full three-lock order/no inversion; generic independent profiles/target completeness; exact fields/signatures/nil/error/refusal; all20 planned IDs wired; Stage B postimplementation; exact six+four no expansion/no gopls/public/D-R/CALLS_ONLY drift.\" / ∀p, Accept(p) ⇒ ExactRevision(p, acf563e7) ∧ SourcesMatch(p,{lease-source-V2,C15-two-stage,generic-amendment,blocked-v1,blocked-v2,source/write-set}) ∧ RecomputedDepsChecksumsStatus(p) / ∀r∈RawBuffers, OneManagerSubledger(r) ∧ ReserveBeforeCopy(r) ∧ NoLeaseEscape(r) ∧ AtomicSingleOwnerTransfer(r) ∧ TerminalConvergenceRelease(r) ∧ LockOrder(r)=L₁≺L₂≺L₃ ∧ ¬LockInversion(r) / Components(p)=SixNamedComponents ∧ |Components(p)|=6 ∧ AliasCount(p)=0 / ∀q∈Profiles, Independent(q) ∧ TargetComplete(q) ∧ Fields(q)=ExactFields ∧ Signatures(q)=ExactSignatures ∧ NilErrorRefusal(q)=ExactContract / WiredIDs(p)=PlannedIDs₂₀ ∧ Stage(p)=B_Postimplementation ∧ Scope(p)=SixPlusFour ∧ ¬Drift(p,{Expansion,gopls,Public,D-R,CALLS_ONLY}) / ∃h, Disposable(h) ∧ Fresh(h) ∧ CompileOK(h) ∧ VetOK(h) ∧ AllCallSitesOK(h) ∧ PrivateVisibilityOK(h)\n§ properties complete? yes\n§ independence: each property has an admissible counterexample that preserves the other five: wrong revision/provenance; custody violation; component/alias mismatch; profile/API mismatch; wiring/scope drift; or failed independent harness.\nRetained properties: property [1]: \"∀p, Accept(p) ⇒ ExactRevision(p, acf563e7) ∧ SourcesMatch(p,{lease-source-V2,C15-two-stage,generic-amendment,blocked-v1,blocked-v2,source/write-set}) ∧ RecomputedDepsChecksumsStatus(p)\"; property [2]: \"∀r∈RawBuffers, OneManagerSubledger(r) ∧ ReserveBeforeCopy(r) ∧ NoLeaseEscape(r) ∧ AtomicSingleOwnerTransfer(r) ∧ TerminalConvergenceRelease(r) ∧ LockOrder(r)=L₁≺L₂≺L₃ ∧ ¬LockInversion(r)\"; property [3]: \"Components(p)=SixNamedComponents ∧ |Components(p)|=6 ∧ AliasCount(p)=0\"; property [4]: \"∀q∈Profiles, Independent(q) ∧ TargetComplete(q) ∧ Fields(q)=ExactFields ∧ Signatures(q)=ExactSignatures ∧ NilErrorRefusal(q)=ExactContract\"; property [5]: \"WiredIDs(p)=PlannedIDs₂₀ ∧ Stage(p)=B_Postimplementation ∧ Scope(p)=SixPlusFour ∧ ¬Drift(p,{Expansion,gopls,Public,D-R,CALLS_ONLY})\"; property [6]: \"∃h, Disposable(h) ∧ Fresh(h) ∧ CompileOK(h) ∧ VetOK(h) ∧ AllCallSitesOK(h) ∧ PrivateVisibilityOK(h)\"\n§ ground complete\n\nPresumed: “lease-source V2,” “C15,” and “generic amendment” denote the exact package-local source artifacts named or linked by the qualification package.\nRevised if: the package manifest identifies different canonical repository paths or revisions.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_086e788cb8bf6932016ace512957808191aab423162a51a904\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning repository state inspection using git commands**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_086e788cb8bf6932016ace519f78ec8191a2f5e96bae623612\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqzlGmz5_eR-soSbI-jJTon-XHU8lzGZh0s0qmG4j5NbsmoDPrALvqjGWDNuBHXERxnvOcbESBfX_19oAt9X52EHAnPuifWuYV087zJahpgJfnO30ivU00OElJRkfben4ptnL0j_f1cWzidrAFfvA8dAmle7GiAvAwZWIv_-2xvjoDdo4APm61pDx_Ey_2VlJxGW2ZlG77l3igsXRdR-8rQRIbRDDELhn1NNLDYhC8NmcHK_z2dcnOAMnyDh537azfDc22yno4H3CrPlE1OxhZ9Qb0E5vg4iKVeHQIo7537tkSJyfESWZuXi5YrngMPD