{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a856f367-42c9-454","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_L8TYyjqNgGQx9fIr583OAI4S|fc_086e788cb8bf6932016ace5230bf04819194fe0d8b0a136b91","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nid: 20260918153914-6083\ntitle: 'Source index: DASL 2026–27 requirements package and SurveyUpdates2027 implementation'\ntype: observation\nstatus: reviewed\ntags:\n    - nais\n    - dasl\n    - requirements\n    - annual-data-entry-change\n    - source-index\ncreated: 2026-09-18T15:39:14.044086Z\nmodified: 2026-10-08T01:47:07.381726-07:00\n---\nfreshness: aging (5 days ago — may need recheck)\n\n\n\n## Sources\n\nA read-only September 18, 2026 inspection covered `/Users/schwa/Downloads/DASL2026-2027Requirements.zip` (SHA-256 `5fa92769f41bbdda2d5f561a12a9189ca29bc2e1334d7de874cff527354636c5`, 2,357,064 bytes). The archive was extracted only to `/tmp` and contained:\n\n- `daslrequest.md`, an export of Linear issue DAS-207, “DASL 2026-2027 changes”;\n- `UpdatesToYearsExperienceDASL2027.docx`;\n- `MASTER 2026-2027 DASL updates.xlsx`;\n- `DASL_Data_Entry_2025-2026 v3.xlsx`;\n- `DASL_Data_Entry_2025-2026 v4.xlsx`; and\n- `DASL_Data_Entry_2025-2026 v4.1.xlsx`.\n\nThe inspection also compared the package with `SQL_2005/NAIS_DATA/Other Scripts/SurveyUpdates2027/` at DASL commit `82fd9d1e5cc3a13dbe257b3f592f8aaaa168a44f`. That directory contains 14 ordered scripts from cleanup and collection preparation through `9-CAIS-CA.sql`.\n\n## Issue evidence\n\nThe DAS-207 export identifies the issue as Done, High priority, Feature, created April 15 and updated June 22, 2026, with linked work `NAISorg/dasl#191`. It instructs implementers to apply the DOCX’s years-of-experience changes to all administrator positions, including association roles, and to Teacher Salaries by Experience. The initial request says not to change or add Advancement until further notice; later thread entries describe Advancement corrections, Joy’s review, authorization to move to production, deployment, and association enablement.\n\n## Boundary\n\nThe archive is participant-authored requirements and issue-history evidence. The Git checkout is retained source evidence. Together they support requirement-to-script lineage but do not independently verify production execution, database state, approval authority, or runtime behavior. The original archive remains outside Git and is treated as confidential NAIS material.\n\n## Links\n\n- [[20260821151130-4130|Hilary describes an annual DASL variable-governance process led by Joy]] [supports] {draft} — The 2026–27 package provides concrete artifact evidence consistent with the stakeholder-described annual variable-governance process, without confirming authority or deployment.\n\n## Backlinks (3)\n\n- [[20260918153914-2908|SurveyUpdates2027 maps the 2026–27 package into administrator, teacher, Advancement, and CAIS-CA metadata changes]] [grounded-by] {draft} — The pinned SurveyUpdates2027 scripts and matched requirement artifacts ground the implementation mapping.\n- [[20260918153914-9435|The DASL 2026–27 workbook revisions stage corrections while largely preserving variable identity]] [grounded-by] {draft} — The four archived workbook versions and their stable-ID/comment comparison ground the staged revision history.\n- [[20260918153914-9524|DASL 2026–27 reframes experience as ordinal year-in-role and year-teaching]] [grounded-by] {draft} — The inspected DOCX, DAS-207 export, workbooks, and pinned SQL scripts ground the 2026–27 ordinal-year semantic changes.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791906353704},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:45:53.705Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
