08ece26d7c1bca3f26e2ceb761e02e77b2|422d413c63ede254ab3b8004e9cb58aec083b1c470da2b28c92084d378c5a2a5|480446a4372c7fb04f694840320ffdf3ee29da89e9c4e6423ac261916068ca5b|51590290aea507a4972547c0923647c52d1c657fdecdfbb3aa6244ba5a417347|645cf06e35e54bc3fe5a827bc0f6a4156c2b23e5739d70d2b012c5c1884ae894|7069d8601cb76101ee1a2c7886f223d0a6119e74b76891d3dd49f35117cb0736|75e32e98aaf21d7ec04d26d13fd202699b4bf6ad466688edb8f70231835a14e7|7f46d76e8acde79c1eec46102632bd6db557ac394d329b31b68c9697abbd4ea2|a3ec11a555246160475c5519e29735fc4f86ce88eeef053bd0f97c88e4221102|b1bf63296afd47f73f2be7e8a9c70db37f0ce77677b5ddf38a8b3a15fcba77d3|b3846db09b2b683ea536a8d6ddcdf3c5ff7408b0c4f6e0097656a4f7a2e16800|c2d3d4696cd315f18b986c14afd02a5ed642d7a99c2888ae172177a48f5ff1bc|c730d1a3978f99c2de26d634266e05a0909a0d5662eee7e86889f7b7603cb5aa|d3ed276e5de20a331b277b63638f7bc5ef05a45c9366a06ece882bb90502ac20|ddbbfd7184803b94919684bb5762ef16309986b1d5b091d650c1e05a9b578779\tone terminal winner clears aliases/bytes and releases every lease exactly once\tNOT_APPLICABLE_PREIMPLEMENTATION\tPLANNED_ARCHITECTURE_OBLIGATION_ONLY; no NECESSARY/REUSE classification\n  → [[20261010201159-8643|Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20261012145659-8845|Integration receipt: three isolated plans converge on evidence-first DataVista Labs exposure planning]] [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791906420603},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:47:00.604Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a856f367-42c9-454","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e19115d57f0e4556baffd5dcea264431|fc_086e788cb8bf6932016ace527372d081918a0de33ac536aa6d","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"==> /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-generic-directional-calls-profile-amendment-go-v1/AMENDMENT.md <==\n10:This amendment freezes provider-neutral directional CALLS semantics separately from provider bindings. It supersedes only gopls-specific semantic assumptions in the directional CALLS qualification architecture. It does not revoke, rewrite, or weaken the accepted opaque raw-custody/32 MiB architecture or its accepted production/test write-set amendment.\n11:\n12:Two generic profiles are independent contracts:\n13:\n14:- `CALLS_LSP_INCOMING_EXACT_V1`, canonical domain `lsp-trace.adr0011.calls.lsp.incoming.exact.v1`;\n15:- `CALLS_LSP_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1`, canonical domain `lsp-trace.adr0011.calls.lsp.outgoing.exact.v1`.\n16:\n17:Two provider bindings are independent contracts:\n18:\n  → [[20261010201159-8643|Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20261010195608-9082|Integration receipt: Correct and independently rereview additive qualified-CALLS ADR0011 amendment]] [possibly relevant]\n15:- `CALLS_LSP_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1`, canonical domain `lsp-trace.adr0011.calls.lsp.outgoing.exact.v1`.\n16:\n17:Two provider bindings are independent contracts:\n18:\n19:- `CALLS_GO_GOPLS_INCOMING_EXACT_V1`, binding only to `CALLS_LSP_INCOMING_EXACT_V1`;\n20:- `CALLS_GO_GOPLS_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1`, binding only to `CALLS_LSP_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1`.\n21:\n22:Incoming does not inherit outgoing and outgoing does not inherit incoming. A provider binding may narrow provider/runtime/toolchain/workspace/evidence eligibility, but cannot add, delete, reinterpret, relax, or replace generic direction semantics, identity fields, occurrence accounting, terminal distinctions, completeness rules, diagnostics, or review obligations. Equal bytes or shared environment artifacts permit content-addressed reference only, never semantic, evidence, review, acceptance, or GO inheritance.\n23:\n  → [[20261010201159-8643|Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260922153414-9145|Integration receipt: fake process-target returns empty outgoing calls unlike qualified live gopls]] [possibly relevant]\n22:Incoming does not inherit outgoing and outgoing does not inherit incoming. A provider binding may narrow provider/runtime/toolchain/workspace/evidence eligibility, but cannot add, delete, reinterpret, relax, or replace generic direction semantics, identity fields, occurrence accounting, terminal distinctions, completeness rules, diagnostics, or review obligations. Equal bytes or shared environment artifacts permit content-addressed reference only, never semantic, evidence, review, acceptance, or GO inheritance.\n23:\n24:## 2. Generic incoming contract\n25:\n26:`CALLS_LSP_INCOMING_EXACT_V1` is provider-neutral LSP call-hierarchy acquisition with these exact semantics:\n27:\n28:1. A target callee is established before preparation under an independently identified target-selection contract.\n29:2. `textDocument/prepareCallHierarchy` is a separate ordered transaction. Its complete ordered result and selected zero-based item ordinal are retained. Selection must be deterministic and target-bound; missing, null, empty, no-match, ambiguous, malformed, partial, stale, substituted, foreign, or over-limit preparation selects nothing.\n30:3. The selected prepared item is passed byte-identically, or through an explicitly qualified exact semantic-preservation rule, to `callHierarchy/incomingCalls`. Re-encoding alone never proves original-byte identity.\n  → [[20260827012030-5178|Corpus-eligibility orientation selects a bounded shared-artifact manifest or exact blocker]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20261010201159-8643|Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan]] [possibly relevant]\n--\n65:- exact language/toolchain/build flags/module/workspace files and immutable locators or bytes;\n66:- exact repository revision, dirty-state proof, workspace root, target files and target-set identity;\n67:- exact managed session/generation, limits, privacy/retention policy, request/response custody, terminal/accounting records, evidence manifest, and independent review.\n68:\n69:`CALLS_GO_GOPLS_INCOMING_EXACT_V1` binds Go/gopls incoming evidence only to `CALLS_LSP_INCOMING_EXACT_V1`. `CALLS_GO_GOPLS_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1` binds Go/gopls outgoing evidence only to `CALLS_LSP_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1`. No binding may inherit another binding’s provider correctness, occurrence ledger, target-set accounting, diagnostic, review, acceptance, or GO. Shared immutable artifacts require independent relevance, freshness, exact-profile binding, and role verification.\n70:\n71:## 6. Target-set-relative completeness only\n72:\n73:Completeness is relative only to a named immutable target set and named acquisition policy. It never establishes repository, workspace, source-graph, runtime, behavioral, language, provider-family, or production completeness.\n  → [[20261010201159-8643|Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260922153414-9145|Integration receipt: fake process-target returns empty outgoing calls unlike qualified live gopls]] [possibly relevant]\n--\n149:\n150:Future work, if separately authorized, must proceed in this causal order:\n151:\n152:1. independently review this amendment candidate and issue the exact token only for its bytes;\n153:2. freeze and review `CALLS_LSP_INCOMING_EXACT_V1` generic contract fixtures/evidence;\n154:3. independently freeze and review `CALLS_LSP_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1` generic contract fixtures/evidence;\n155:4. bind and qualify `CALLS_GO_GOPLS_INCOMING_EXACT_V1` against the accepted incoming generic profile and its own target set/evidence;\n156:5. independently bind and qualify `CALLS_GO_GOPLS_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1` against the accepted outgoing generic profile and its own target set/evidence;\n157:6. only then request a separate implementation/test-write authorization under the unchanged raw-custody architecture and frozen write-set.\n  → [[20261010201159-8643|Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260922153414-9145|Integration receipt: fake process-target returns empty outgoing calls unlike qualified live gopls]] [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791906420603},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:47:00.604Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a856f367-42c9-454","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_99231eb8ef8d4e978926021cd6463e9a|fc_086e788cb8bf6932016ace527372d08191a1063151370aef0f","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"==> /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-directional-raw-custody-c15-two-stage-contract-v2/README.md <==\n32:5. no absent source is semantically classified.\n33:\n34:Stage A completeness is architecture-obligation completeness, not source-semantic completeness and not implementation GO.\n35:\n36:### Stage B — POST-IMPLEMENTATION\n37:\n38:After an implementation is separately authorized and committed, a canonical source enumerator must regenerate actual rows from an exact committed implementation source manifest. Actual row IDs are source-derived and must not reuse planned IDs. `STAGE_B_ACTUAL_CLASSIFICATION.tsv` is intentionally header-only before implementation.\n39:\n40:An independent review then classifies every actual row as exactly `NECESSARY`, `REUSE`, `FALSE_POSITIVE`, or `UNRESOLVED`. `UNRESOLVED=0`, exact source-manifest verification, deterministic duplicate/omission checks, and complete planned-to-actual correction lineage are required before any later `IMPLEMENTATION_GO` can be considered.\n  → [[20260918153914-6083|Source index: DASL 2026–27 requirements package and SurveyUpdates2027 implementation]] [possibly relevant] [read]\n  → [[20260731022209-9191|Ontology: DASL approval is an unresolved evidence coordinate, not a grounded repository state.]] [possibly relevant]\n--\n42:Planned-to-actual lineage is carried separately in `STAGE_B_PLANNED_ACTUAL_LINEAGE.tsv` and is many-to-many and correction-safe: disappeared plans are recorded as `DISAPPEARED` with an empty actual successor set; one plan producing several actual rows is `SPLIT`; several plans producing one actual row is `MERGED`; ordinary correspondence is `REALIZED`; unplanned actual rows are `EMERGENT`. Each lineage record contains complete planned/actual predecessor and successor sets. Actual identities always derive from committed source path, symbol, operation, component, and `backing_identity_rule`. Planned IDs remain lineage evidence and never become actual row IDs.\n43:\n44:## Gate ordering\n45:\n46:The requested two-stage token qualifies these contract bytes only. It is not interface GO, RED/test GO, implementation GO, production admission, activation, commit authority, or permission to mutate production/tests. Interface and RED remain blocked until the two-stage contract receives its exact review token. Implementation remains blocked until separately authorized after interface and RED gates. Stage B cannot run until a committed implementation exists, and this package does not authorize creating one.\n47:\n48:Normative order:\n49:\n50:1. `TWO_STAGE_CONTRACT.md`\n  → [[20261010201159-8643|Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260826235337-9258|Corrective orientation selects actual inspection of five frozen provenance routes]] [possibly relevant]\n\n==> /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-directional-raw-custody-c15-two-stage-contract-v2/REVIEW_REQUEST.md <==\n12:2. identity accounting enumerates 47 exact preserved v1 IDs plus one newly introduced planned reservation architecture obligation, distinguishes their provenance, explains the generator cause, and proves duplicates/omissions `0` for the `47 + 1` denominator;\n13:3. Stage A existing rows are restricted to Manager accounting ownership, account lifecycle, lease APIs/transfer capabilities, terminal cleanup, and nearby nonreusable leases;\n14:4. Stage A future rows use only `PLANNED_RESERVATION`, `PLANNED_COPY`, `PLANNED_ALIAS`, `PLANNED_TRANSFER`, and `PLANNED_RELEASE`, with exact proposed bindings and exact stable predecessor row IDs or `GENESIS`; predecessor closure has cycles, missing predecessors, and branches equal to zero;\n15:5. Stage A completeness is identity and architecture-obligation completeness, not source-semantic completeness;\n16:6. Stage B requires canonical enumeration from an exact committed implementation source manifest, source-derived actual IDs including `backing_identity_rule`, independent `NECESSARY|REUSE|FALSE_POSITIVE|UNRESOLVED` classification, and `UNRESOLVED=0` before any later implementation GO;\n17:7. a separate exact lineage table handles `REALIZED`, `DISAPPEARED`, `SPLIT`, `MERGED`, and `EMERGENT` with complete planned/actual predecessor-successor sets, including an explicitly empty actual successor set for `DISAPPEARED`, without reusing planned IDs;\n18:8. source and run checksums verify and generated outputs reproduce byte-for-byte;\n19:9. interface GO, RED GO, implementation GO, production admission, activation, and commit authority all remain false.\n20:\n  → [[20261010201159-8643|Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260814153537-3616|The July 2017 DASL planning artifact is an agenda for usage, infrastructure, interoperability, and UX decisions.]] [possibly relevant]\n17:7. a separate exact lineage table handles `REALIZED`, `DISAPPEARED`, `SPLIT`, `MERGED`, and `EMERGENT` with complete planned/actual predecessor-successor sets, including an explicitly empty actual successor set for `DISAPPEARED`, without reusing planned IDs;\n18:8. source and run checksums verify and generated outputs reproduce byte-for-byte;\n19:9. interface GO, RED GO, implementation GO, production admission, activation, and commit authority all remain false.\n20:\n21:Record reviewer identity/revision, source-manifest result, run-manifest digest, reconciliation/count result, Stage A schema/completeness result, Stage B and correction-lineage result, immutable-evidence result, and exact token or one blocker.\n22:\n23:The token qualifies contract bytes only. It does not authorize implementation or tests.\n24:\n25:Current disposition: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`.\n  → [[20261010201159-8643|Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260725001014-8818|The NAIS pitch committed to phased dual-running migration under NAIS go-no-go authority]] [possibly relevant]\n\n==> /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-directional-raw-custody-c15-two-stage-contract-v2/TWO_STAGE_CONTRACT.md <==\n33:### Stage A completeness\n34:\n35:`PREIMPLEMENTATION_COMPLETE` requires all 47 preserved v1 identities plus one newly introduced planned reservation architecture obligation accounted, duplicates `0`, omissions `0`, planned predecessor closure with cycles/missing predecessors/branches `0`, all six components covered by reservation/copy/alias obligations, whole-acquisition transfer present, and terminal convergence release present. The model-reported 48 is unpinned because no exact full adjudicator output is available to copy and hash-prove. Completeness says nothing about actual implementation source semantics.\n36:\n37:## Stage B: POST-IMPLEMENTATION\n38:\n39:Stage B begins only from an exact committed implementation revision and canonical source manifest. It does not accept line-0, absent-source, or planned rows as actual rows.\n40:\n41:The canonical actual row ID is:\n  → [[20260826200941-1958|Post-row-21 completion orientation selects row-1 metadata candidate-gap adjudication]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260814161613-4019|DASL Release to Reporting is documented as a per-collection-part transfer governed by annually revised runbooks.]] [possibly relevant]\n35:`PREIMPLEMENTATION_COMPLETE` requires all 47 preserved v1 identities plus one newly introduced planned reservation architecture obligation accounted, duplicates `0`, omissions `0`, planned predecessor closure with cycles/missing predecessors/branches `0`, all six components covered by reservation/copy/alias obligations, whole-acquisition transfer present, and terminal convergence release present. The model-reported 48 is unpinned because no exact full adjudicator output is available to copy and hash-prove. Completeness says nothing about actual implementation source semantics.\n36:\n37:## Stage B: POST-IMPLEMENTATION\n38:\n39:Stage B begins only from an exact committed implementation revision and canonical source manifest. It does not accept line-0, absent-source, or planned rows as actual rows.\n40:\n41:The canonical actual row ID is:\n42:\n43:```text\n  → [[20260814161613-4019|DASL Release to Reporting is documented as a per-collection-part transfer governed by annually revised runbooks.]] [possibly relevant]\n  → [[20260826200941-1958|Post-row-21 completion orientation selects row-1 metadata candidate-gap adjudication]] [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791906420603},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:47:00.604Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
