"Observation 8 — accepted-source comparisons confirm the two generic profile IDs/domains and independence language, target-set-relative completeness, and Stage B’s postimplementation-only boundary. The Stage A source table exposes a likely blocker: its 20 rows require exact proposed symbols such as `reserveDirectionalPrepareFrameV3`, `copyDirectionalPrepareFrameV3`, and `aliasDirectionalPrepareFrameV3`, whereas V3 currently declares generic component methods and merely stores the 20 row IDs as constants. I will mechanically reconcile all 20 IDs, required symbols, and references before concluding.\n\nskip-related: 20260913000638-8253 20260913000506-2499 20261010201159-8643 20260921234531-6240 20261012145659-8845 20261010195608-9082 20260922153414-9145 20260827012030-5178 20260731022209-9191 20260826235337-9258 20260814153537-3616 20260725001014-8818 20260826200941-1958 20260814161613-4019 — related-note suggestions concern other reviews or domains and are not needed for this exact byte-level reconciliation.\n\nGate: Search rationale: ADR0011 Stage A 20 planned obligation IDs exact symbol binding requirements — check retained knowledge before running a custom repository reconciliation script.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_086e788cb8bf6932016ace528109b48191bbe2f9d8ca2aee3f\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e4888e6f5d924eb583f28da2eeafc54b|fc_086e788cb8bf6932016ace528567108191987e23e23b558842","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"nn list --search \"ADR0011 Stage A 20 planned obligation IDs exact symbol binding requirements\" --json --fields id,title,score,match_reason","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":8943,"output":643,"cacheRead":86400,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":288,"totalTokens":95986,"cost":{"input":0.035772,"output":0.012860000000000002,"cacheRead":0.03456,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.083192}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791906420606,"responseId":"