xt","text":"Selected note: “Post-consolidation orientation selects a staged exact-24 evidence-routing pilot.”\n\nSelected because: the score is `1` and the match_reason is `\"title, body, outbound\"`.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_086e788cb8bf6932016ace5289e0bc819194a1adc945b13fe8\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5b1abc633a6d405db2b88a544e189c86|fc_086e788cb8bf6932016ace528a2f9481918fc9314f042c1ce9","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"nn show 20260826214655-4711","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":1015,"output":94,"cacheRead":95232,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":12,"totalTokens":96341,"cost":{"input":0.00406,"output":0.0018800000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0380928,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.044032800000000004}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791906438700,"responseId":"resp_086e788cb8bf6932016ace52878fe48191b76d841dfe95936b","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"minimal"},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:47:24.850Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a856f367-42c9-454","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5b1abc633a6d405db2b88a544e189c86|fc_086e788cb8bf6932016ace528a2f9481918fc9314f042c1ce9","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nid: 20260826214655-4711\ntitle: Post-consolidation orientation selects a staged exact-24 evidence-routing pilot\ntype: model\nstatus: reviewed\ntags:\n    - nais\n    - orient\n    - scope-rationalization\n    - feature-inventory\n    - evidence-routing\nexpires_when: the staged exact-24 pilot reaches its terminal, or denominator, provenance, schema, or cost assumptions fail\ncreated: 2026-08-26T21:46:55.825394Z\nmodified: 2026-08-26T15:01:00.291563-07:00\n---\nfreshness: stale (47 days ago — revalidate before using as evidence of current conditions; this does not imply the historical note should expire)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n## Outcome\n\nFresh complete Stage 1–4 orientation selects a staged exact-24 evidence-routing pilot sourced only from the consolidated snapshot’s exact 205-ID `NOT_ASSESSED` set. Status: `SELECTED_FOR_CRAFT`. No implementation, evidence gathering, source/runtime inspection, or worker dispatch occurred.\n\n## Stage 1 — position\n\nScopeRationalization is the active receiver. Consolidation closed integration-state uncertainty but not semantic uncertainty. The decision frontier is whether candidate-specific evidence can be routed at sufficient qualifying/partial/non-actor-facing yield and sufficiently low parent integration cost to justify wider work. Acceptance, value, priority, representativeness, production truth, and canonical authority remain `UNKNOWN`.\n\n## Stage 2 — failure model\n\nAccess-rich failure is semantic overreach; access-poor failure is treating no located evidence as evidence of absence; schedule-compressed failure is hiding invalid worker envelopes and parent normalization cost; direction-change failure is non-replayable sampling. Controls are exact retained spans, typed outcomes, separate authority, schema-before-semantics validation, deterministic snapshot lineage, and phase-timed parent cost.\n\n## Stage 3 — execution ledger\n\nCompared six candidate classes: coupled exact-24 worker pilot; parent-only 24 baseline; frozen-case contract pilot; paired parent/worker topology sample; routing-method comparison; no action. Each retained Phase 1 receiver, unresolved question, material terminal difference, evidence tier, duplicate boundary, direct/option consequence, smallest artifact, maximum cost, security method, disposition, and overturning observation. The full method comparison was narrowed to exception-only fallback.\n\n## Stage 3.5 — recovery\n\nRecovered the 24-row pilot into a staged flow: deterministic 24-of-205 selection; six-row parent preflight; continue only under frozen informative-yield and stable-vocabulary predicates; two worker schema canaries; valid workers route disjoint nine-row partitions; one fallback route only for initial searched-no-evidence cases; parent-only semantic reconciliation. Parent cap is 150 minutes plus bounded read-only worker effort. Every gate is terminal and `automatic_continuation=false`.\n\n## Stage 4A — selection\n\nThe staged exact-24 pilot passes role, privacy, safety, reachability, duplicate, evidence/authority-ceiling, and stop gates. Four positions were compared: receiver-backed work exists; option-building work also exists; transport-only probe is too weak; no action leaves reachable scaling uncertainty unresolved. The staged pilot has greatest decision value relative to total cost because it embeds the parent preflight and canaries rather than funding separate pilots. Strongest alternative is parent-only preflight; it loses because bounded worker partitions additionally measure schema validity and scaling economics.\n\nSelection falsifiers: semantic/cherry-picked selection; source IDs outside exact 205; unavailable exact retained spans; invalid canary; unstable preflight vocabulary; all-six searched-no-evidence; projected parent cost above 150 minutes; equivalent retained pilot; or authority/source boundary failure.\n\n## Stage 4B — controlled plan\n\nFreeze exact predecessor path/bytes/hash and 205 IDs; deterministic nonsemantic 24 selection; exact 6/9/9 disjoint ownership; one primary outcome per row (`QUALIFYING_USER_EVIDENCE`, `PARTIAL_USER_EVIDENCE`, `POSITIVE_NOT_ACTOR_FACING`, `SEARCHED_NO_EVIDENCE`, or `PROHIBITED_INFERENCE_REQUIRED`); `FEATURE_HYPOTHESIS_REACHABLE` only as a derived all-four-user-dimensions subset; candidate-specific evidence tier/provenance/span receipts; schema-valid unnormalized worker envelopes; parent-only semantic adjudication; exact before/after ID-set reconciliation; and phase-timed parent cost.\n\nMeasure: `NOT_ASSESSED` reduction; qualifying evidence yield; partial-evidence yield; feature-hypothesis reachability; positive non-actor-facing evidence; searched-no-evidence; prohibited-inference outcomes; schema-valid worker canaries/receipts; parent validation, reconciliation, exception, and integration minutes. Honest denominators follow executed rows if a gate stops early.\n\nBefore mutation run Bar Craft and verify `/Users/schwa/dev/nais-discovery`. Red-first guards cover predecessor drift, denominator/partition errors, semantic selection, outcome overlap, unsupported reachability, missing provenance, evidence-absence inference, malformed receipt acceptance/normalization, worker semantic integration, wrong ID-set delta, missing cost receipt, authority/identity promotion, and terminal behavior.\n\nAllowed terminal: `OUTCOME_PROGRESS | BLOCKER_LOCALIZED | NO_CHANGE`. Always `automatic_continuation=false`. Pilot success does not authorize another batch or wider expansion.\n\n\n## Implementation terminal\n\nCommit `92bc7aa` implemented the staged exact-24 pilot package. The exact 205-ID snapshot was hash/byte/commit locked; deterministic ID-only sampling produced 24 unique candidates with exact 6/9/9 ownership. The six-row parent preflight completed with 6/6 `PROHIBITED_INFERENCE_REQUIRED`: candidate-relevant retained context existed, but candidate-specific semantic correspondence would require prohibited non-lexical inference. No row left `NOT_ASSESSED`.\n\nExactly two disjoint worker jobs were launched. Both failed before canary submission with `No API key found for amazon-bedrock.` Therefore schema-valid canaries and receipts were 0/2, neither partition was accessed, no parent normalization or replacement occurred, and the frozen canary gate stopped execution. Honest executed denominator is 6/24; qualifying, partial, reachable, positive non-actor-facing, and searched-no-evidence yields are 0/6; prohibited inference is 6/6; `NOT_ASSESSED` reduction is 0; parent cost is 33 minutes.\n\nP1-P15 were observed red then green; fifteen isolated mutations pass; deterministic pilot SHA-256 is `1d4016230e6f8cf6ffce7885e493382b505aeb7242ab0c58b7b537e2e18ff749`; Python compilation, diff check, compactness (147 lines), and full retained lifecycle pass. Terminal `BLOCKER_LOCALIZED`; `automatic_continuation=false`. Fresh orientation is required before provider repair, worker retry/replacement, parent-only completion, or another batch.\n\n## Links\n\n- [[20260826212636-8752|Post-Phase-A orientation selects one compact correction-preserving provisional inventory snapshot]] [extends] {draft} — Follows the completed correction-preserving snapshot by selecting the separately oriented exact-24 evidence-routing pilot over its exact 205-ID NOT_ASSESSED complement.\n- [[20260811212231-4787|Protocol: run four-stage Bar independent-discovery orientation]] [grounded-by] {draft} — Records the complete goal-led, worth-based four-stage orientation that selected and bounded the staged pilot.\n- [[20260826204708-7924|Post-f3cfa69 orientation selects a 14-candidate parent-controlled parallel classification pilot]] [grounded-by] {reviewed} — The prior exact-14 pilot supplies the observed invalid-envelope failure that this pilot must test with fail-fast schema canaries and no parent normalization.\n- [[20260826175715-6117|Post-capability correction orientation selects an exact-30 user-evidence reachability join]] [grounded-by] {reviewed} — The exact-30 reachability join supplies the retained evidence vocabulary and all-four-user-dimensions reachability boundary reused by this pilot.\n\n## Backlinks (1)\n\n- [[20260826220728-6959|Provider-corrected orientation selects one configured exact-24 worker retry]] [extends] {draft} — Reopens only the provider-auth blocker with an explicit authenticated child-model canary while preserving the exact pilot state.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791906444849},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:47:24.850Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
