  - Therefore the claims “all 20 planned IDs bind exact declarations” and “constants adjacent to their declaration symbols” are false.\n\n2. **Replace the count-only Stage A verifier with exact reconciliation.**\n   - `go.count('privateStageA') >= 21` does not verify:\n     - the exact 20-ID set;\n     - uniqueness;\n     - ID-to-symbol correspondence;\n     - symbol existence;\n     - declaration adjacency;\n     - call-site wiring.\n   - Require exact comparison against `STAGE_A_PLANNED_OBLIGATIONS.tsv`.\n\n3. **Expand the disposable harness to cover the claimed call shapes.**\n   - The fresh rebuild compiled and vetted successfully, and external access to private identifiers correctly failed.\n   - But `compilePlannedV3` does not independently instantiate all claimed RED/C15/race shapes. Missing explicit coverage includes component-specific planned symbols, arithmetic overflow, broad nil/invalid combinations, distinct transfer-failure preservation, callback refusal, lock-order/inversion surfaces, and genuine race-shaped calls.\n   - Sequential duplicate release is not a race-call-shape check.\n\n### Checks that passed\n\n- Exact HEAD: `acf563e7708095d8a32c809b49d97c7432d49b03`.\n- All V3 checksums recomputed exactly.\n- Generic amendment, lease-source V2, two-stage C15, blocked V1/V2, and five existing production-source pins match.\n- V1 and V2 each remain byte-identical to their own immutable manifests.\n- Only the 11 V3 package files are untracked; no production/test source changed.\n- Six component identities and zero charged alias components are represented.\n- Generic incoming/outgoing identities and target-relative completeness agree with the amendment.\n- Stage B remains postimplementation.\n- Six-production-plus-four-new-test write-set is preserved.\n- Fresh package compilation, compile-only tests, and `go vet` passed.\n- Private visibility was independently confirmed by intended external compilation failures.\n- No Go/gopls provider semantics were found in the declarations.\n\nThe package remains correctly bounded as `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`, but the exact acceptance token cannot be issued for these bytes.\n\nPhase result:\n  id: adr0011-v3-independent-audit\n  status: completed\n  result: REVISE\nPhase end.\n\n## Model interpretation\n\n- Treated “wired” as requiring an exact ID-to-required-symbol binding, not merely copying IDs into constants.\n- Treated harness claims as requiring explicit compile-time call shapes rather than general methods invoked through a component loop.\n- Managed LSP evidence was not used to elevate completeness or acceptance.\n\nGaps:\n- Runtime custody, lock ordering, and exact-once release remain future implementation obligations; declaration stubs cannot prove them.\n- The package is untracked, so its bytes are not attributable to HEAD itself.\n\nImproved framing: Accept V3 only when exact Stage A reconciliation and the independently rebuilt harness both prove the declaration-level contract without relying on substring counts.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_086e788cb8bf6932016ace52e38474819182daf3b0da8bafd1\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":5351,"output":1599,"cacheRead":100352,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":813,"totalTokens":107302,"cost":{"input":0.021404,"output":0.03198,"cacheRead":0.040140800000000004,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0935248}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1791906509820,"responseId":"resp_086e788cb8bf6932016ace52cf3c6481918ced881d83bc09fa","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"minimal"},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:49:05.853Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
