eded by exact reconciliation and fresh-run results.\n[full]: \"cover everything important\" → \"The response addresses every named element of the subject at one level of depth\" as applied here: exact-20 wiring, every claimed call-shape class, prior requirements, hashes, and status will be checked.\n[ground]: \"derive what correctness means before acting\" → \"The response must produce a 'Ground properties:' block before any test, implementation step, tool call, or task reasoning begins\" as applied here: the corrected package is evaluated against the formal properties below.\nWhat it requires here: freeze exact set equality and binding, fresh executable verification, and preservation of all prior accepted boundaries.\n[presume]: \"make a call and move on\" → \"The response selects the most plausible option wherever the subject leaves a choice open and proceeds on it instead of stopping to request approval or clarification\" as applied here: a unique disposable harness directory will be selected and discarded as evidence-only.\nWhat it requires here: identify any reversible operational choice and its contradiction trigger.\n[atomic]: \"one thing per step\" → \"The response makes one observable change per step, where a step is a single unit of change\" as applied here: each verification stage will produce a separately attributable result.\nWhat it requires here: do not conflate static ID reconciliation with compilation or semantic call-shape coverage.\nWithout witness, the conclusion would not expose its basis; without full, a requested call-shape class could be omitted; without ground, corrected bytes could silently weaken the contract; without presume, a harmless disposable-path choice could stall execution; without atomic, a combined failure would obscure which gate failed.\nDerived stance complete.\n\nGround properties:\nInterpretation: GO is valid only if the corrected untracked V3 package at the exact requested worktree satisfies both the frozen interface contract and every explicitly requested fresh verification; the accessible boundary is package/source bytes plus independently generated read-only/disposable outputs.\nproperty [1]: GO(p) ⇒ Bijection(TSV₂₀,Constants₂₀,Symbols₂₀) ∧ Adjacent ∧ Defined ∧ Referenced ∧ Extras=∅ ∧ Missing=∅\n§ formality check: property [1]: \"GO(p) ⇒ Bijection(TSV₂₀,Constants₂₀,Symbols₂₀) ∧ Adjacent ∧ Defined ∧ Referenced ∧ Extras=∅ ∧ Missing=∅\" — formal\n§ minimality: property [1]: minimal — most specific sub-term: \"TSV₂₀\"; candidate relaxation: replace \"TSV₂₀\" with any subset; rejected: the request requires exact reconciliation of all 20 rows.\nproperty [1a]: GO(p) ⇒ Bijection(TSV₂₀,Constants₂₀,Symbols₂₀)\nproperty [1b]: GO(p) ⇒ Adjacent ∧ Defined ∧ Referenced ∧ Extras=∅ ∧ Missing=∅\n§ formality check: property [1a]: \"GO(p) ⇒ Bijection(TSV₂₀,Constants₂₀,Symbols₂₀)\" — formal\n§ formality check: property [1b]: \"GO(p) ⇒ Adjacent ∧ Defined ∧ Referenced ∧ Extras=∅ ∧ Missing=∅\" — formal\n§ split test: property [1]: \"GO(p) ⇒ Bijection(TSV₂₀,Constants₂₀,Symbols₂₀) ∧ Adjacent ∧ Defined ∧ Referenced ∧ Extras=∅ ∧ Missing=∅\" ⇔ (property [1a]: \"GO(p) ⇒ Bijection(TSV₂₀,Constants₂₀,Symbols₂₀)\" ∧ property [1b]: \"GO(p) ⇒ Adjacent ∧ Defined ∧ Referenced ∧ Extras=∅ ∧ Missing=∅\"); property [1a] — falsified by one wrong ID; property [1b] — falsified by one unreferenced exact symbol; these falsifiers are independent.\n§ constraint coverage: property [1]: covers {exact 20 ID-to-symbol mapping, adjacency, definition, reference, no extras, no missing}\n§ atomic: property [1]: \"GO(p) ⇒ Bijection(TSV₂₀,Constants₂₀,Symbols₂₀) ∧ Adjacent ∧ Defined ∧ Referenced ∧ Extras=∅ ∧ Missing=∅\" — candidate split rejected: these jointly constitute the requested exact reconciliation.\n\nproperty [2]: GO(p) ⇒ ∃h,Fresh(h) ∧ Compile(h) ∧ Vet(h) ∧ Covers(h,{PerSymbol,Overflow,NilInvalid,TransferFailure,CallbackRefusal,Lock,Race})\n§ formality check: property [2]: \"GO(p) ⇒ ∃h,Fresh(h) ∧ Compile(h) ∧ Vet(h) ∧ Covers(h,{P